{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485597247,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk0MDIyNzkwNQ=="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1485622289,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTg1OTI3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1235#issuecomment-275859276"},"message":"Well... I hear you, but it is  `git remote add` ... All the custom diversions from API semantics people might be familiar with is IMHO not benefiting... Having said that I am yet to check what configuration changes this command does ATM in comparison to create-sibling, or what could be moved into it","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487262862,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDM4MzE4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1235#issuecomment-280383180"},"message":"OK, so you want to keep `add_sibling`. So be it (although the argument is lame: `git remote add` is one of many subcommands for `remote`).\n\nThis means we need another command: `(re)configure-sibling` it needs to do all things \"what to fetch\", \"what to push\", \"what to prefer\".... that came up in the context of `update` and `publish`. This is no static configuration that is only done once when added. The command's interface needs to be duplicated in `add-sibling`, and in `create-sibling`, to some degree also in `create-sibling-github`. Don't have a full list of related issues, but one is #712.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487263986,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDM4OTEwMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1235#issuecomment-280389103"},"message":"I lean towards renaming `add_sibling`. However, if @yarikoptic wants an explicit `add_sibling` for consistency with `git`, it should call `configure_sibling` internally with a safe guard switch to make sure the sibling doesn't exist already. It's just a short cut and I don't really care whether we have it.\n\nRe GitPython's fetch needs a `remote.\u003cname\u003e.fetch` entry: This is true only, if no refpec was passed. Just saying to not let that potentially confusing statement be uncommented. :-)\n\nOtherwise: I agree on what `configure-sibling` should be able to do.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1487267753,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDQwNzIyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1235#issuecomment-280407227"},"message":"I am ok to the plan of action such as\n- get a sparkling new configure_sibling\n- keep add_sibling as a shim with a proper deprecation warning.  We really should start adding those warnings and Changelog entries on what has changed in the API -- I keep running into being unable, sometimes with silent/absent error (see #1309), to perform what I could have done before, and needing to dig/ask/etc to figure out what I should do now.  Thus I would vote against renaming a command to another one to merely improve some semantical notion without even leaving any deprecation trail.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487268818,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDQxMjEwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1235#issuecomment-280412107"},"message":"Re deprecation warning/changelog: I agree. It's a point, we should start to care for.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1487278769,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDQ1ODU0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1235#issuecomment-280458541"},"message":"we might then want to adopt instead of my ad-hoc one -